{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And I gave</b>. It is possible that the matter of this verse is joined with what follows it, namely that he searched in wisdom — and likewise the sense of לתור is like 'to search the earth to see matters of delight' (cf. Ecclesiastes 2:3) — and the roots of all deeds, even though it is a bad matter, because man occupies himself with something that will not avail. The explanation of לענות בו is from the matter of ענין, and some say it is from the word ענוי, and he says that like it is אני עניתי מאד and וענה גאון ישראל. More correct is that וענה is from לא תענה ברעך, and likewise עניתי like ויען איוב, and what follows it indicates upon it: אני אמרתי בחפזי, and likewise ישמע אל ויענם — יענה בם, or he will return a reply to them. And when he occupied himself to see the roots of deeds, he found that they are הבל ורעות רוח. And the explanation of תחת השמים will be like תחת השמש. And it is possible that he hinted in the word תחת השמים, like תחת השמש, at the upper sphere, where all the host of the heavens is, and the wisdom of the mystery of the stars upon the forty-eight forms of the sphere. And after he looked into the way of wisdom to know the root of all deeds that are generated from the power of the heavens, he saw that it is a bad and evil matter, because of the shortness of men's understanding to enumerate the generators, let alone all generated things, and there is no number to the heavenly cohorts; and the ancients could not recognize except one thousand twenty-two. And this is what indicates it: that he said תחת השמים, עת לכל זמן, and likewise the second, which is in the verse: תרתי בלבי."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "The phrase אלף ושנים ועשרים ('one thousand twenty-two') is translated hyper-literally; it may refer to the count of fixed stars recognized by the ancients (Ptolemy's catalog lists 1,022). The closing citations (עת לכל זמן; תרתי בלבי) are rendered as they stand; their referents are cryptic."}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:26:58.546057453Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}